# configflux-9pjy.5: core-contract verification + hardening suite for the
# product-compile resource budget (ADR-0039 §8). Pins graceful-degradation
# monotonicity (derived memo_cap non-increasing as the budget shrinks),
# byte-neutrality (budget=None and a memory-only budget produce
# byte-identical artifacts — no cluster_size derivation, no fixture
# rotation), and the progress / serde / precedence hardening contracts. The
# adaptive-shrink-count half of the core contract is verified with an
# injected deterministic RSS sampler inside the ccm_emitter unit tests (run
# by compiler_test), the only scope that can reach the test-only sampler
# seam; the CLI --max-rss-mb/--max-threads round-trip lives in main.rs's own
# #[cfg(test)] (run by compiler_cli_test). All assertions are deterministic
# — no real /proc RSS or wall-clock is asserted.
rust_test(
    name = "scenario_resource_budget_test",
    size = "small",
    timeout = "short",
    args = ["scenario_resource_budget_tests::"],
    crate = ":compiler_lib",
)

